Subject: [PATCH] fix: Lost Isles re-run fixes, mine retest, vehicle combat
 rework (F-219)

Second goblin (Gobmine) run from Kezan through the Lost Isles; I-385 mine Overseer PASS.
- accept from the NEAREST giver in our phase (Farewell, For Now: Thrall's ship vs the Overlook)
- accept timeout: talk to the giver (gossip hello) and ask again
- spellhit that is really the click's own spell (Good Help is Hard to Find 66306): click instead
- stranded on a dead-end partial path (seabed after Irresistible Pool Pony): straight step at the target
- swimmers (Mechashark) drive straight like flyers; ground vehicles stay on the navmesh
- REVERT "make the vehicle the mover on boarding": re-anchoring at interact.find's stale summon
  spot broke the Mechashark (no damage); re-anchor only when >15 yd apart
- sustained bar casting from 2000 HP up (a 3.7k naga out-healed spaced shots); kite targets
  10+ levels above us (Gallywix) at the bar's longest range instead of trading in melee
- bar_kinds: TRIGGER_SPELL into a damage spell = "cone" weapon (Machine Gun 73456 -> 74958)
- bar_timing: per-spell cooldown + range from the DBC (SpellRange floats are raw IEEE bits)
- dogfight(): flying vehicle vs flying targets (The Pride of Kezan) - re-aim at the nearest
  fighter every 0.5 s in short hops, Machine Gun cone within 45 yd, rockets only in range and
  off cooldown. NOT yet exercised live (Gobmine was past 25066 when it landed).

